      "content": "Their arguments regarding \"moral decay\" were heavily influenced by prevailing Victorian sensibilities about social roles and purity. They asserted that mixing social spheres would lead to the erosion of traditional moral codes within both communities. Specific concerns often pointed to interracial contact leading to perceived challenges to established family structures, particularly concerning gender roles, which they felt were sacrosanct to white society. Essentially, the claim was that integrated environments would foster social habits deemed inherently \"corrupting\" according to their rigid social hierarchies.",
